    // #314: a fourth value per row, measured on the authored level's own 12 rolls (cell 2.5,18.5
    // floor 0.00 with its lamp at -1.00; the pit camera was found in 12 of 12 rolls, so this is not
    // a vacuous record). PIT-CELLS 204 and PIT-MEAN 0.287 sit inside the generated levels' range.
    // OOB-ERA/OOB-NONCLIMB record ZERO because level 3 has NO non-climb wrong-band cell to leak
    // through (0 of 0): the row reports its population, so a zero population reads as zero
    // population rather than as a pass.
    const RECPIT = refRecord('alt', 'PIT-MEAN', 'num', [0.289, 0.347, 0.335, 0.316]);   /* #548 EVERY ROOM OWNS ITS AIR onto main-after-#199/#585 (main 7116e68), MEASURED on the combined tree: L1 0.338 -> 0.347 and L2 0.317 -> 0.335, both printed by this row's own clause (4), while L0's 0.289 and L3's 0.316 hold TO THE DIGIT in the same run - the authored plan runs no part of the every-room rule, so L3 is the scope control. This is mean delivered light in pit cells, and the direction is UP, which is the same physical claim this PR's CZBAND-LIGHT re-key makes: a room with four units of air has more room between its lamps and its roof for the spill to reach the band term's own one-quantum reach. WHAT MAKES THIS A GEOMETRY RE-KEY AND NOT A RELIGHT is printed beside it in the same run: worst cross-band alpha fraction 0.036 / 0.000 against MAXFRAC 0.05, lip delivery 0.995 / 1.000 against floors 0.950 / 0.931, 0 dark pits of 190 / 194 / 211 / 204 with every population count matching its record, and `no column is lit from a band ABOVE it` / `…BELOW it` both reading 0 open cells on all four levels - so a source's OWN band reaches a little further into a pit, and no light crosses a floor. The 0.005 tolerance is unchanged; no threshold, window or vacuity floor moved. */   // #413 re-record L0/L1, L2/L3 byte-for-byte unchanged: a fitting hung over a room delivers light to the band it hangs over, and on the two generated levels with pits adjacent to tall rooms some of that land reaches a pit floor's column through the band term's own one-quantum reach. Mean delivered light in pit cells 0.262 -> 0.272 (L0) and 0.294 -> 0.325 (L1); the dark-pit COUNT this row also asserts stays 0 of 190 / 0 of 194, and `alt`'s wrong-band census still reads 0 cells lit from a band above or below their own, so this is a source on its own band doing what a source does, not a leak across one. No threshold touched (the 0.005 tolerance is unchanged) and the two levels with no tall room over a pit did not move.
